This is an AI generated patch to fix issue with deadlock and forced reset to fix
network.

This will restore the 30 day uptime instead of doing a hard reset every day.

The low uptime issue happened around CopyFail and Fragnesia fix was submitted.

At around the time a deadlock happens, the kernel will output to dmesg the
following:

[73768.919526] wlp0s18f2u4: Limiting TX power to 127 (127 - 0) dBm as advertised by <redacted>
[74893.329552] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: read register 0xaa failed with -110
[74893.869270] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: rtw_usb_reg_sec: reg 0x4e0, usb write 1 fail, status: -110
[74894.926330] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: read register 0x770 failed with -110
[74895.982336] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: read register 0x774 failed with -110
[74896.526379] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: write register 0x76e failed with -110
[74897.582483] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: read register 0x1cc failed with -110
[74899.186462] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: write register 0x1f0 failed with -110
[74899.730467] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: write register 0x1d0 failed with -110
[74909.778768] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: write register 0x9a4 failed with -110
[74990.768155] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: rtw_usb_reg_sec: reg 0x4e0, usb write 1 fail, status: -110
[74992.369198] rtw88_8821cu 2-4:1.0: rtw_usb_reg_sec: reg 0x4e0, usb write 1 fail, status: -110

When analyzing commit 6b96494, I noticed that there was a freed memory but no
mutex unlock and the code reviewer mindlessly okaying the commit into master.

Code reviewers should consider the mutex unlocking whenever there is a memory
free before rashly approving the commit.

The driver has been broken for more than 3 months.

When the deadlock happens, all network consuming commands (eg. ping, nmtui)
will deadlock.  Also, it is not possible to unload the driver while
deadlocking.  nmtui will refuse to deactivate or rescan for Wi-Fi.
It is also likely to cause OpenRC to halt before restart.  It may cause
compiler to halt because it affects maybe the IO scheduler.  So I am forced
to reset the computer.  I tried unsetting CONFIG_CFG80211_DEFAULT_PS and
setting CONFIG_USB_AUTOSUSPEND_DELAY=-1 for the kernel config, and the
following for /etc/modprobe.d/rtw88.conf:

options rtw88_core disable_lps_deep=Y support_bf=Y
options rtw88_pci disable_aspm=Y
options rtw88_usb switch_usb_mode=N
options usbcore autosuspend=-1

and it didn't fix the deadlock and frequent disconnect issue before this patch.

For the frequent disconnect because of the recent driver security fixes, it
will cause the DNS to mess up.  Some domains will work and others not.  I have
to disconnect and reconnect more than usual after uploading.  Since applying
this AI generated patch, I am doing fewer manual resets and no forced resets
after uploading through nmtui.

Patch status:  testing

